{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463290",
      "title": "Lists & Keys",
      "lectureOrder": 49,
      "videoOrder": 44,
      "sourceHash": "4cbf3625c7103b655533c66d476b7e46dd6016c7acf33da08dcb425e53251ae6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.83,
          "en": "We're almost done with VF and V-for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.83,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "but here's one important addition related to V-for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 11.6,
          "en": "which you have to be aware of since...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.6,
          "end": 16.22,
          "en": "Well, you can see strange bucks if you're not aware of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.22,
          "end": 19.76,
          "en": "Let's say our goal and index here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.76,
          "end": 23.52,
          "en": "is actually in a paragraph, inside of the list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.52,
          "end": 24.663,
          "en": "So it looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.07,
          "end": 31.07,
          "en": "Hence if I, Master Vue here, we see it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.15,
          "end": 35.447,
          "en": "Now let's say besides that, we also have input here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 39.333,
          "en": "where we can enter some text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.35,
          "end": 42.2,
          "en": "And let's also make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.2,
          "end": 44.15,
          "en": "we can actually enter something here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.15,
          "end": 47.78,
          "en": "because right now, if I reload and add this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.78,
          "end": 49.73,
          "en": "you'll see whenever I click in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.73,
          "end": 53.14,
          "en": "I also click on the list item and therefore it's removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.14,
          "end": 56.3,
          "en": "We can avoid this by adding a click listener here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.3,
          "end": 58.603,
          "en": "where we add the stop modifier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 61.72,
          "en": "You learned about event modifiers before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.72,
          "end": 63.94,
          "en": "and this stops propagation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.94,
          "end": 66.83,
          "en": "So it makes sure that when we click on the input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.83,
          "end": 69.24,
          "en": "the click is only processed there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.24,
          "end": 72.793,
          "en": "and the disc click event on the list item is not triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.03,
          "end": 77.67,
          "en": "We don't have to specify any code that should be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.67,
          "end": 81.06,
          "en": "if all we wanna do is stop the event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.06,
          "end": 85.25,
          "en": "So now if I reload, we can Master View,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.25,
          "end": 87.3,
          "en": "click in there and type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.3,
          "end": 91.07,
          "en": "But I didn't do that to just show you the stop modifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.07,
          "end": 92.75,
          "en": "even though it's good to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.75,
          "end": 95.52000000000001,
          "en": "Instead of let me show you a strange bug",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 98.10300000000001,
          "en": "that you can experience with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.44,
          "end": 104.44,
          "en": "I will also add, Finish the course as another goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.09,
          "end": 111.09,
          "en": "and now I will actually type in here something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.3,
          "end": 114.72999999999999,
          "en": "So in the first goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 114.72999999999999,
          "end": 117.913,
          "en": "And now click on it so that this goal gets deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.91,
          "end": 120.18,
          "en": "And isn't that strange?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.18,
          "end": 123.74,
          "en": "Something is still there on the second goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 123.74,
          "end": 125.12,
          "en": "The first one was deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.12,
          "end": 127.49,
          "en": "So the new first one is the old second one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.49,
          "end": 129.87,
          "en": "and it kept something around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.87,
          "end": 133.58,
          "en": "Might look like a cool feature, but it's actually a buck.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 133.58,
          "end": 135.04,
          "en": "This might become more obvious",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.04,
          "end": 137.82999999999998,
          "en": "if I reload and try this again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.82999999999998,
          "end": 140.54,
          "en": "Master Vue, Finish the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.54,
          "end": 142.63,
          "en": "and now let's do it the other way round.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.63,
          "end": 144.99,
          "en": "Let's enter something here in the second goal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.99,
          "end": 146.863,
          "en": "and remove the first one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 150.53,
          "en": "Now Finish the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.53,
          "end": 154.11,
          "en": "had something in this input field a few seconds ago",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.11,
          "end": 156.3,
          "en": "until we deleted the first goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.3,
          "end": 158.34,
          "en": "Now the old second goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.34,
          "end": 160.82,
          "en": "Finish the course, is the new first goal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.82,
          "end": 164.78,
          "en": "but it lost the input which we had in these input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.78,
          "end": 167.82999999999998,
          "en": "And this is definitely not what you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.82999999999998,
          "end": 170.74,
          "en": "You could argue that this is a niche scenario,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.74,
          "end": 174.42000000000002,
          "en": "but the problem that causes this is actually a bigger one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.42000000000002,
          "end": 176.82999999999998,
          "en": "which can also lead to performance issues",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.82999999999998,
          "end": 179.43,
          "en": "if you don't fix it properly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.43,
          "end": 181.3,
          "en": "The problem here is simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.3,
          "end": 185.12,
          "en": "Vue updates the list when you add and remove items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.12,
          "end": 187.3,
          "en": "it renders the list in the real Dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.3,
          "end": 189.61,
          "en": "and updates it as required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.61,
          "end": 194.48,
          "en": "And it tries to do that such that it optimizes performance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.48,
          "end": 198.62,
          "en": "That also means that it reuses Dom elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.62,
          "end": 203.62,
          "en": "So if we have two goals here, two Dom elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.01,
          "end": 206.34,
          "en": "and I delete the first one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.34,
          "end": 209.64,
          "en": "Vue will actually not re-render the entire list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.64,
          "end": 212.55,
          "en": "It will also not delete the first Dom element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 212.55,
          "end": 214.35,
          "en": "and move to the second one around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.35,
          "end": 218.62,
          "en": "Instead it basically takes the content of the second element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.62,
          "end": 221.62,
          "en": "and moves it into the first Dom element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.62,
          "end": 226.62,
          "en": "And that explains why if I enter some text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.26,
          "end": 230.88,
          "en": "that text is lost if I delete the first element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.88,
          "end": 234.13,
          "en": "Because the first Dom element is not actually removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.13,
          "end": 236.42000000000002,
          "en": "instead the content of the second one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.42000000000002,
          "end": 239.15,
          "en": "And with content, I mean the dynamic content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.15,
          "end": 241.4,
          "en": "So this part with the curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.4,
          "end": 244.243,
          "en": "is moved into the old first Dom element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.38,
          "end": 248.46,
          "en": "The input element in the first Dom element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.46,
          "end": 250.28,
          "en": "is still the old one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.28,
          "end": 254.96,
          "en": "because the entire list item is still the old first element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 254.96,
          "end": 258.31,
          "en": "Just the dynamic content was moved around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258.31,
          "end": 260.58,
          "en": "and that's why we lose the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.58,
          "end": 262.47,
          "en": "we had on the second element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.47,
          "end": 264.47,
          "en": "when the content of the second element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.47,
          "end": 267.623,
          "en": "moves to the old first element's, Dom element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 271.663,
          "en": "I hope I could make it clear what the problem here is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.08,
          "end": 276.14,
          "en": "Now this occurs because Vue reuse this elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.14,
          "end": 278.43,
          "en": "which generally is good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.43,
          "end": 283.08,
          "en": "But sometimes it needs to be able to tell elements apart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.08,
          "end": 286.43,
          "en": "Now the problem is since they all have the same element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 286.43,
          "end": 290.3,
          "en": "the same Dom element, they are all LI elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.3,
          "end": 293.85,
          "en": "There is no unique identification criteria",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.85,
          "end": 296.02,
          "en": "for every rendered Dom element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.02,
          "end": 298.01,
          "en": "Yes, the content is different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.01,
          "end": 300.81,
          "en": "but thankfully Vue is not going ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.81,
          "end": 303.77,
          "en": "and comparing all the content with each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 303.77,
          "end": 306.86,
          "en": "That would be super performance intensive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.86,
          "end": 308.49,
          "en": "Instead, long story short,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 308.49,
          "end": 311.38,
          "en": "there is a simple extra attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 311.38,
          "end": 315.08,
          "en": "which is a non default HTML attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 315.08,
          "end": 320.05,
          "en": "which you can add on elements on which you also use V-for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.05,
          "end": 322.443,
          "en": "And that's the key attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.29,
          "end": 324.67,
          "en": "The key attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.67,
          "end": 328.83,
          "en": "I'm going to say it again is not a default HTML attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.83,
          "end": 333.34000000000003,
          "en": "instead it is an attribute understood and detected by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 333.34000000000003,
          "end": 336.47,
          "en": "It's optional, but it is a good idea to add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 336.47,
          "end": 338.49,
          "en": "whenever you're using V-for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.49,
          "end": 341,
          "en": "And actually you will also later in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 341,
          "end": 344.39,
          "en": "see that there are many scenarios where you must use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 344.39,
          "end": 348.68,
          "en": "So it's already a good habit to start using it on all items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 348.68,
          "end": 350.96,
          "en": "where you're using V-for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 350.96,
          "end": 355.02,
          "en": "And key, once a unique identification criteria",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 355.02,
          "end": 357.9,
          "en": "for every item it's outputting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 357.9,
          "end": 362.06,
          "en": "Therefore, we wanna bind it to a dynamic value with V-bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 362.06,
          "end": 365.09,
          "en": "or the short end, just a colon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 365.09,
          "end": 366.91,
          "en": "And now in here, we need something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 366.91,
          "end": 369.523,
          "en": "that uniquely identifies every goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 370.71,
          "end": 373.92,
          "en": "You might be inclined to say the index does that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 373.92,
          "end": 376.56,
          "en": "because every goal has its own index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 376.56,
          "end": 380.46,
          "en": "But well, keep in mind that if I have two goals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 380.46,
          "end": 382.53,
          "en": "and I delete the first one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 382.53,
          "end": 385.8,
          "en": "the old second one now has index zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 385.8,
          "end": 389.13,
          "en": "The index doesn't really belong to the goal content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 389.13,
          "end": 391.5,
          "en": "The index is always the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 391.5,
          "end": 395.49,
          "en": "The first item always has index zero, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 395.49,
          "end": 399.07,
          "en": "So the index isn't strictly attached to the element value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 399.07,
          "end": 400.49,
          "en": "in the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 400.49,
          "end": 403.95,
          "en": "So the index is not really a good thing to use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 403.95,
          "end": 407.64,
          "en": "Instead in this case, we could use the goal text itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 407.64,
          "end": 409.88,
          "en": "Of course we could enter the same goal text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 409.88,
          "end": 412.94,
          "en": "more than once here, but let's assume that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 412.94,
          "end": 414.293,
          "en": "Then goal is good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 415.15,
          "end": 418.38,
          "en": "More realistic examples, would be IDs",
          "zh": ""
        },
